\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A2}{\ignorespaces Regen event on the 15-state truth model; the first \SI {5}{\second } of the \SI {60}{\second } simulation is shown (the response is in steady state for the remainder). Top: bus-voltage deviation. Bottom: share deviation. The bus traces are nearly indistinguishable, and not because the event is rail-dominated (the clamp is touched for well under $1\,\%$ of the evaluation horizon): the excursion is set by the peak braking current both controllers reach, which is a property of the demand and of the plant, not of the droop architecture.}}{25}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
